      "data": {
        "value": "<p><strong>INDICATION &amp; SAMPLE INFORMATION</strong></p>\n<p>History not received</p>\n<p><strong>METHOD</strong></p>\n<p>PCR, Fragment Analysis</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Type of Transcript</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Area</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Area under the NPM1 positive peak</td>\n<td>0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Area under the NPM1 normal peak</td>\n<td>93363</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>RESULT</strong></td>\n<td><strong>NOT DETECTED</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Allelic Ratio<br>(Area of Mutant / Area of wild type)<br>As per ELN recommendation 2017</strong></td>\n<td>&lt;0.01 (as per detection limit)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div><strong>Allelic frequency</strong></div>\n<div><strong>[Area of Mutant /(Area of mutant + wild type) x100]</strong></div>\n</td>\n<td>&lt;1% (as per detection limit)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><br><strong>HISTORICAL DATA</strong></p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Date</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Allelic Ratio</strong></td>\n<td><strong>% Reduction from Baseline</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>06-02-2024</td>\n<td>&lt;0.01 (as per detection limit)</td>\n<td>Baseline value not provided</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://radiology-flabs.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/464d5c56d62600a82e2a.png\" data-cke-saved-src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"><br><strong>NOTE</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This test detects all types of insertion/deletion NPM1 mutations by fragment analysis on a capillary electrophoresis system</li>\n<li>This allelic ratio sensitivity of this test is 0.01.</li>\n<li>Test conducted on Whole blood / Bone Marrow</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>COMMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>Evaluation of NPM1 is recommended in cases of cytogenetically normal AML as detection of these mutations in the absence of a FLT3 mutation or presence of FLT3 mutation with low allelic ratio (&lt;50%) confers a favorable prognosis confers a good prognosis and thus NPM1 mutations should always be interpreted with results of FLT3 mutations. NPM1 mutations are class II mutations which impair&nbsp;hematopoietic differentiation and subsequent apoptosis. They do not occur in combination with the recurrent cytogenetic abnormalities in AML and may represent a biologically distinct entity. NPM1 Exon 12 insertion/deletion mutations are more prevalent in AML. More than 10 types of NPM mutations have been reported; types A(956dupTCTG), B(960insCATG), D (960insCCTG) together constitute &gt;95% of the mutations.<br><br><strong>USES</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>This is a quantitative assay for monitoring response to therapy.</li>\n<li>For prognostic evaluation of AML.</li>\n<li>Monitoring of Minimal Residual Disease (MRD).</li>\n</ul>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
